# Paged KV, u8 keys / i4 values: the MIXED stage runs on micro-SDPA

# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of
# patches/0003-0019 (verified: applies cleanly on the pristine pin with exactly that
# series). Campaign u8i4-prefill-price (arcint DESIGN.md sections 7.0.2ar/7.0.2as).
#
# The price this removes. With the chunk held at 128 on the 16 GiB card (coder, no
# offload), u8:i4 prefill cost +55 % of u8's time at 37,707 tokens and +90 % at 71,727
# (DESIGN 7.0.2ar), and the profiler could not name the kernel. The cause, by reading
# and now by removal: patches/0009 made supports_micro_sdpa() decline every key/value
# pair whose packing classes differ, so the served pairing (u8 keys by channel, the
# plugin's default, with i4 values by token) fell from the microkernel
# attention path to the generic paged_attention_opt multi_tokens kernel for every chunk
# after the first. Decode was never affected (patches/0010's split read kernel).
#
# What changes (three files, one gate split):
#   sdpa_gen_micro.cpp  The generator sets the VALUE operand's type and layout from the
#                       value precision (patches/0008's VALUE_CACHE_PRECISION) instead of
#                       the key's: problem_vs.Ta_ext becomes u4/i4 whenever the value
#                       cache is four-bit; the JIT layout constants are computed per side
#                       (the key keeps upstream's three layouts, the value is packed
#                       head/2 + inline scale/zp -- the layout pa_kv_cache_update_ref.cl
#                       already writes for IS_INT4_V); IS_INT4_K_CACHE / IS_INT4_V_CACHE
#                       are emitted per side, IS_INT4_KV_CACHE keeps its symmetric
#                       meaning. VAL_ELEMENTS_PER_BYTE, which the kernel uses to advance
#                       the value pointer across key chunks, is derived from the value
#                       CACHE's precision on the mixed stage rather than from the
#                       new-token input port (which is not four-bit under u8 keys):
#                       without that the pointer overshot by two from the second 128-key
#                       chunk on -- measured as NaN for every query whose causal context
#                       passed 128 keys, and only those.
#   sdpa_micro.cl       The five blocks gated on IS_INT4_KV_CACHE split into their key side
#                       (ldk, ldkq, the K block pointer and its scales) and value side
#                       (ldv, ldvq, the V block's inline scales), each on its own macro;
#                       IS_INT4_KV_CACHE is still emitted for the symmetric case, with no
#                       consumer left in the kernel source.
#   paged_attention_opt.cpp  supports_micro_sdpa() admits eight-bit keys with four-bit
#                       values; four-bit keys with eight-bit values still decline (no
#                       layout on either kernel). Four-bit values under BY_TOKEN keys are
#                       declined too: measured on the staged tree as NaN past 128 keys
#                       with the patch's own test, not diagnosed, and not what the plugin
#                       serves by default (key_cache_quant_mode defaults to BY_CHANNEL,
#                       execution_config.cpp; arcint sets nothing).
#
# Red first, then green (ov_gpu_unit_tests on the staged tree, the 16 GiB card, the
# production units running beside the test binary, 2026-09-05):
#   paged_attention_u8i4_mixed_micro_test.mixed_stage_serves_u8_key_i4_value_on_micro_sdpa
#   (new; three shapes: 25 queries over a 34-token past, 25 over 128, 300 over 64; u8 keys
#   BY_CHANNEL, u4 values; the u4 mixed micro regression's exactly-representable fill and
#   its 1e-2 tolerance against the float reference; asserts "sdpa_micro" in the kernel
#   dump). On the 0019 tree: FAILED, the dump naming paged_attention_opt__multi_tokens.
#   With the patch: PASS, 3/3. The older regression_paged_attention_asymmetric_prefill
#   cases (patches/0015: 128 new tokens over a 2,048 and a 1,024 past, u8-K/i4-V, random
#   data) now run on micro-SDPA and match the reference; their assertion that micro-SDPA
#   "stays declined" is turned around, being the routing this patch changes. The whole
#   paged-attention set with the u4 micro, asymmetric decode, bounded-partials and
#   symmetric-u4 suites: 276 of 277 pass, one pre-existing skip. patches/0010's decode
#   test keeps asserting that "sdpa_micro" is absent from its kernel dump, and still
#   passes: the decode (single-token) stage has no microkernel variant; this patch
#   changes the MIXED stage's selection only.
#
# Served, on the recipe-built plugin (pin + 0003-0020, staged over the packaged runtime),
# 16 GiB card, coder, no offload, chunk 128, the price window's own prompts:
#   37,707 tokens: u8:i4 459.0 t/s (82.2 s) against u8 456.8 t/s -- before, 295.1 against
#   456.8 (+55 %); 71,727 tokens: u8:i4 401.0 t/s (178.9 s) against u8 397.5 -- before,
#   209.3 against 397.9 (+90 %). Parity at both depths. The u8:i4 32-token outputs are
#   byte-identical to the generic path's at both depths; the Pruefstand through the
#   u8:i4 server at 37,707 tokens: 10/10 (479 tokens). Decode, one sample each: u8:i4
#   31.4 / 28.1 t/s at 32 tokens against u8's 33.3 / 30.8 -- a report. No fault line.
#
# Not changed: the write kernel, the decode read kernel (patches/0010), the PREFILL stage
# (which reads the new tokens' f16 inputs, not the cache), the value cache layout, the
# auto-fit ceiling. The values stay four-bit in VRAM throughout: the microkernel unpacks
# them in registers, which is the constraint the campaign's invariants state.
#
# Upstream: not yet filed.
